# Cloudflare Pages redirects. Parsed by Pages, never served as an asset.
#
# CANONICAL HOST: https://steckercheck.de (apex, no www)
#
# www.steckercheck.de cannot be redirected from this file. Cloudflare Pages
# matches _redirects rules on the path only and lists domain-level redirects as
# unsupported:
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/#advanced-redirects
#
# The apex host is therefore declared in rel=canonical, og:url, the hreflang
# links, sitemap.xml and llms.txt, and the www duplicate has to be closed with
# one Single Redirect rule in the Cloudflare dashboard:
#
#   Rules -> Redirect Rules -> Create rule
#   If:   http.host eq "www.steckercheck.de"
#   Then: Dynamic redirect
#         URL: concat("https://steckercheck.de", http.request.uri.path)
#         Status: 301
#         Preserve query string: on
#
# CANONICAL PATHS: extensionless, no trailing slash.
# Pages already answers .html and trailing-slash requests with a 308. These
# rules keep the same URL policy in the repository instead of relying on a
# platform default, and answer 301 for the six paths that exist.

/index.html                  /                       301
/800-watt-2000-wp.html       /800-watt-2000-wp       301
/schuko-oder-wieland.html    /schuko-oder-wieland    301
/balkonkraftwerk-kaufen.html /balkonkraftwerk-kaufen 301
/impressum.html              /impressum              301
/datenschutz.html            /datenschutz            301
